00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
“Follow the stars.” 

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
I heard the voice of Nunyati in my head. 

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
“They will guide you. They have guided migrants for generations. 

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Otherwise, don’t trust anyone. Just yourself. You are on your own now, Mawusi. We willow warblers are solo travellers. That’s the only way to be safe.”

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Back then, I remember listening to him in total disbelief. How could I ever know my way in total darkness, without a map, without someone to show me the way? 

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:07.000
I envied the sparrows, the geese, who travelled in flocks, following the older, more experienced migrants. I was alone. 

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:20.000
And yet, he was right. I realised I knew the way. Without a doubt, I trusted my ancestors’ heritage, and I flew, as fast as the wind. 

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:34.000
How could I ever describe that feeling? That sense of total freedom? That sensation that you are finally meeting your destiny? It was exhilarating. I felt invincible. 

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:43.000
I was racing into the night, further and faster than I had ever gone. Me who had never flown more than a few miles! 

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:57.000
I saw the men’s lights beneath me, those little electric lines of roads and villages, like a spiderweb. They looked so small, so frail. You can’t catch me now, I laughed. 

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:08.000
And then, suddenly, the spiderweb stopped. There was just total darkness. A world of shadows. 

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:22.000
My heart started racing, so I decided to land on a tree at the limit of the men’s kingdom to rest. The sun was rising at the horizon. And then, I saw it.  

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Ahead of me lay an area of unimaginable emptiness. An immense stretch of land that humans had been too terrified to conquer. 

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:42.000
And here I was, a little bird, knowing that my destiny was beneath it. 

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:53.000
The world’s greatest desert. The Sahara.
